---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactLinks from '../components/ContactLinks.astro';
---

<Base title="Matthew Rossi">

  <div class="home-header">
    <div class="home-header-name">
      <h1>Matthew Rossi</h1>
      <span class="location">Brooklyn, New York</span>
    </div>
    <p class="tagline">Senior software engineer transitioning to sustainable urban mobility policy and planning.</p>
    <ContactLinks />
  </div>

  <section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
    <h2 id="about-heading">About</h2>
    <p>I grew up outside Detroit, a place built almost entirely around the car — where the near-total absence of alternatives made the relationship between transportation and daily life hard to take for granted. That early awareness turned into a lasting interest in how cities move people, and what it costs when they can't.</p>
    <p>I spent thirteen years as a software engineer working across fintech, financial services, and cloud infrastructure. That work built an instinct for how complex systems hold together — and where they fail. Reliability, governance, and institutional coordination matter as much as the underlying technology; purely technical solutions run out where policy and planning frameworks aren't there to support them.</p>
    <p>I'm now formalizing that interest through graduate study in sustainable urban mobility, with the goal of working at the intersection of transport policy, systems planning, and data analysis.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="now" aria-labelledby="now-heading">
    <h2 id="now-heading">Now</h2>
    <p>Currently a Senior Software Engineer at <a href="https://www.heroku.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Heroku (Salesforce)</a> in New York, building distributed credential and authorization infrastructure for next-generation cloud platforms.</p>
    <p>Starting autumn 2026, I'll be a full-time student in the <strong>EIT Urban Mobility Master's Programme in Sustainable Urban Mobility Transitions (SUMT)</strong> — a two-year double degree programme. First year at Técnico Lisboa in Lisbon, Portugal; second year at UPC BarcelonaTech in Barcelona, Spain.</p>
  </section>

</Base>
